The issue you flagged is real—`matchesAt` assumes `event.evidence.semanticTextPresent` is always present, but the public `resolveCaptureAtoms` can receive a malformed projection straight from tests or external callers.
Adding the null-guard keeps it fail-closed and prevents the TypeError from leaking into production paths. I ran the golden test after the fix and it still passes, 100% green. No other critical holes found. Ready to ship.
